    "title": "GOD STILL LIVES",
    "creator": "Unknown",
    "chorus": [
      "I hear His voice, ten thousand tongues, The rocks and hills the birds that sing; The rippling brook, all nature tells, That God still lives and all is well."
    ],
    "stanzers": [
      {
        "stanzer": 1,
        "lines": [
          "78 GOD STILL LIVES",
          "Within the heart of every man He strives himself to understand; God’s mighty hand from ages past, Declare His work of righteousness."
        ]
      },
      {
        "stanzer": 2,
        "lines": [
          "From greatest man to infant child, From space afar to grain of sand; ‘Tis written plain, it’s everywhere, That God is real His wondrous power."
        ]
      },
      {
        "stanzer": 3,
        "lines": [
          "I see his power, ten thousand worlds, the order of the universe; Where’ere man goes, God’s gone before, Foundations laid, creation morn."
        ]
      },
      {
        "stanzer": 4,
        "lines": [
          "Tho’ man may go to distant star God’s hand laid out, the parth afar, and lo, returns to earth again, Man can but say, “How great Thou art.”"
        ]
      }
    ]
